is give opening remarks

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.194
on what they, in their work experience,

00:05:05.194 --> 00:05:06.810
what they in their research

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:08.880
and their practice as policy makers

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:10.260
and as people who have been

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.663
engaging in interdisciplinary
conversations,

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:18.830
what they see as gaps in
combining the human side

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.373
and the climate side.

00:05:21.866 --> 00:05:23.940
And then we'll have a discussion
of some of those gaps.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.240
Then we'll come back for five

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.702
relatively longer remarks
from each of the panelists

00:05:30.702 --> 00:05:33.660
on what can we do to
resolve some of these gaps.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.600
Hopefully looking at the problem first,

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:39.660
then responding with solutions
will lead us to some ideas

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:42.110
that wouldn't have occurred
to the four panelists

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.626
just coming in fresh.

00:05:45.626 --> 00:05:47.640
So we're hoping to have
that kind of discussion.

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:50.280
And at the end, leave some time for Q &amp; A.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.170
So I wanna introduce the panel first

00:05:52.170 --> 00:05:53.520
