- Thank you.

00:56:47.322 --> 00:56:51.660
Climate models and we have
less rich economic models

00:56:51.660 --> 00:56:54.783
and I mean it is a cost
question of cost benefit.

00:56:56.001 --> 00:56:57.150
Lemme try, there's a cost of cost benefit,

00:56:57.150 --> 00:56:58.920
where do you start, right?

00:56:58.920 --> 00:57:01.877
Tony has like already the rich model,

00:57:01.877 --> 00:57:03.690
but what is the elements
that you want to put first?

00:57:03.690 --> 00:57:05.800
A few elements like heterogeneous agents

00:57:08.022 --> 00:57:10.350
or you know, like what,

00:57:10.350 --> 00:57:13.650
more capital choices or
something more many sectors.

00:57:13.650 --> 00:57:14.853
Where do you start?

00:57:16.920 --> 00:57:19.020
- I think at least in
the economics literature

00:57:19.020 --> 00:57:22.053
and the general equilibrium
macro literature,

00:57:23.283 --> 00:57:24.745
I think what's been missing,

00:57:24.745 --> 00:57:27.120
